{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771237757542,"sessionID":"ses_39a00e1f2ffeTfoOwyWI4Ya0up","part":{"id":"prt_c65ff5236001xk9KFsfduxpc5y","sessionID":"ses_39a00e1f2ffeTfoOwyWI4Ya0up","messageID":"msg_c65ff36fc001b3ZXstnhlz47qa","type":"tool","callID":"call_9f7c8689ab0f440a926b8129","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","offset":1130},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1130: - Integrated into Game.tsx to toggle settings panel\n1131: - Follows existing patterns for timeout management and cleanup\n1132: - All 341 tests passing\n1133: \n1134: **Technical Decisions:**\n1135: \n1136: - Uses useRef for tap tracking (avoid re-renders)\n1137: - Implements resetTapState function inside useEffect closure for access to refs\n1138: - Configurable threshold zone for corner detection\n1139: - Supports both touch (touchstart) and mouse (click) events\n1140: - Prevents default on touch events to avoid conflicts with game controls\n1141: - Cleanup removes event listeners and clears timeout\n1142: - Time window: 500ms between taps (standard gesture timing)\n1143: \n1144: **Test Coverage:**\n1145: \n1146: - All existing 341 tests continue to pass\n1147: - Gesture detection verified through manual testing\n1148: - Hook follows React best practices for event handling\n1149: \n1150: **Implementation Summary (Export/Import JSON):**\n1151: \n1152: - Implemented Export JSON button in SettingsPanel footer\n1153: - Implemented Import JSON button with hidden file input\n1154: - Export creates downloadable JSON file (gol-expert-settings.json)\n1155: - Import loads JSON file with validation\n1156: - Comprehensive validation for all expert settings parameters\n1157: - Error message display for invalid imports\n1158: - File format: JSON with pretty-printing (2-space indentation)\n1159: - Blob-based file download with URL.createObjectURL\n1160: - FileReader API for file upload\n1161: - All 349 tests passing\n1162: \n1163: **Technical Decisions:**\n1164: \n1165: - Export uses Blob and URL.createObjectURL for download\n1166: - Pretty-printed JSON with 2-space indentation\n1167: - Import validates against all parameter ranges\n1168: - Custom validation function returns detailed error messages\n1169: - Hidden file input triggered via button click\n1170: - Error state managed in component state\n1171: - Invalid settings prevent import with user feedback\n1172: \n1173: **Validation Coverage:**\n1174: \n1175: - Movement detection: centroidHistoryLength (3-10), movementThreshold (0.1-2.0), minClusterSize (1-5)\n1176: - Scoring: moverPointsPerGeneration (1-100), oscillatorPointsPerGeneration (0-20), scoreMultiplier (0.1-5.0)\n1177: - Level generation: baseTimeSeconds (10-120), timeIncrementPerLevel (0-60), baseFlux (5-50), difficultyScalingMode (TIME_ONLY, RESOURCE_ONLY, MIXED, EXTREME)\n1178: - Grid sizing: mobileCellSize (14-24), desktopCellSize (16-28), minVisibleCells (≥1)\n1179: - Audio: enabled (boolean), volume (0-0.5), waveform (sine, triangle, square, sawtooth)\n1180: \n1181: **Test Coverage:**\n1182: \n1183: - All existing 349 tests continue to pass\n1184: - Export functionality verified through manual testing\n1185: - Import functionality verified with valid and invalid JSON files\n1186: - Error handling tested for malformed JSON\n1187: \n1188: ### 5.2 Presets System (LOW - Convenience)\n1189: \n1190: - [x] Implement preset configurations\n1191:   - Easy: Lower difficulty, generous resources\n1192:   - Normal: Balanced gameplay\n1193:   - Hard: Strict time/flux limits\n1194:   - Chaos: Extreme parameters, unpredictable\n1195: - [x] Implement preset selection UI\n1196:   - Dropdown in Expert Settings\n1197:   - Preview preset values\n1198: - [x] Add custom preset support (COMPLETED 2026-02-16)\n1199:   - Allow users to save current settings as preset\n1200:   - Name and save custom configurations\n1201:   - Load and delete custom presets\n1202:   - Custom presets persisted to localStorage\n1203: \n1204: **Dependencies**: Expert settings\n1205: \n1206: **Implementation Summary (Custom Preset Support):**\n1207: \n1208: - Implemented Preset type in src/types/index.ts with four preset options: EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS\n1209: - Implemented src/lib/presets.ts library with applyPreset(), getPresetDescription(), and preset configurations\n1210: - Created four preset configurations with balanced parameter sets:\n1211:   - EASY: Generous Flux (30), longer time limits (90s), lenient scoring (15pt movers, 3pt oscillators), lower movement threshold (0.3)\n1212:   - NORMAL: Balanced Flux (20), standard time limits (60s), standard scoring (10pt movers, 2pt oscillators), standard movement threshold (0.5)\n1213:   - HARD: Limited Flux (15), shorter time limits (40s), strict scoring (8pt movers, 1pt oscillators), higher movement threshold (0.7)\n1214:   - CHAOS: Extreme Flux (10), very short time limits (30s), chaotic scoring (5pt movers, 1pt oscillators), low movement threshold (0.1), larger grid sizing (28px desktop, 22px mobile)\n1215: - Updated SettingsPanel.tsx to include preset selector with description at top of panel\n1216: - Updated SettingsPanel.css with preset section styling\n1217: - Updated createInitialExpertSettings() in src/lib/state.ts to use NORMAL preset by default\n1218: - Added comprehensive test suite with 11 tests covering all presets and edge cases\n1219: - All tests passing (360 total)\n1220: \n1221: **Technical Decisions:**\n1222: \n1223: - Preset type defined as enum-like string union: 'EASY' | 'NORMAL' | 'HARD' | 'CHAOS'\n1224: - applyPreset() performs deep clone using JSON.parse(JSON.stringify()) to prevent mutation issues\n1225: - getPresetDescription() returns human-readable description for each preset explaining the balance and intended difficulty\n1226: - Preset selector placed at top of SettingsPanel for easy access and visibility\n1227: - Preset descriptions use glassmorphism styling with subtle background for readability\n1228: - Default preset is NORMAL for balanced gameplay experience\n1229: - All preset parameters validated against spec-defined ranges\n1230: - Preset application immediately updates all expert settings without requiring panel close/reopen\n1231: - Preset configurations include all expert settings: movement detection, scoring, level generation, grid sizing, and audio parameters\n1232: \n1233: **Test Coverage: 11 tests**\n1234: \n1235: - Preset type definition: 1 test\n1236: - EASY preset configuration: 1 test\n1237: - NORMAL preset configuration: 1 test\n1238: - HARD preset configuration: 1 test\n1239: - CHAOS preset configuration: 1 test\n1240: - applyPreset() deep clone behavior: 1 test\n1241: - applyPreset() applies correct values: 1 test\n1242: - getPresetDescription() returns correct descriptions: 3 tests (EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS)\n1243: - Invalid preset handling: 1 test\n1244: \n1245: **Integration Notes:**\n1246: \n1247: - Presets integrated into SettingsPanel as dropdown selector at top of panel\n1248: - Preset selector onChange handler calls applyPreset() to update expert settings\n1249: - Preset descriptions displayed below selector to explain each preset's characteristics\n1250: - createInitialExpertSettings() now uses applyPreset('NORMAL') for default configuration\n1251: - Preset system works seamlessly with existing settings persistence (localStorage)\n1252: - Users can manually tweak parameters after selecting a preset for further customization\n1253: - Total test count: 389 tests passing (up from 374)\n1254: \n1255: **Implementation Summary (Custom Preset Support - 2026-02-16):**\n1256: \n1257: - Added CustomPreset interface to src/types/index.ts with name, settings, and createdAt fields\n1258: - Implemented custom preset management functions in src/lib/presets.ts:\n1259:   - getCustomPresets(): Retrieve all custom presets from localStorage\n1260:   - saveCustomPreset(name, settings): Save current settings as custom preset\n1261:   - deleteCustomPreset(name): Remove custom preset by name\n1262:   - applyCustomPreset(name): Load and apply custom preset\n1263:   - isCustomPresetNameAvailable(name): Check if preset name is unique\n1264: - Updated SettingsPanel component with custom preset UI:\n1265:   - \"Save as Custom Preset\" button to save current settings\n1266:   - Modal dialog for entering preset name\n1267:   - Custom preset list with Load/Delete buttons\n1268:   - Custom presets added to preset dropdown selector\n1269:   - Error handling for duplicate names and empty names\n1270: - Custom presets persisted to localStorage under 'gol-custom-presets' key\n1271: - Deep copy of settings saved to prevent mutation issues\n1272: - Comprehensive CSS styling for custom preset dialog and list in SettingsPanel.css\n1273: - Added 15 new tests for custom preset functionality (getCustomPresets, saveCustomPreset, deleteCustomPreset, applyCustomPreset, isCustomPresetNameAvailable)\n1274: \n1275: **Technical Decisions:**\n1276: \n1277: - Custom preset names must be unique and non-empty\n1278: - Custom presets stored in separate localStorage key ('gol-custom-presets')\n1279: - Settings deep copied before saving to prevent reference issues\n1280: - preset field cleared from saved custom settings to avoid confusion\n1281: - Custom preset list displayed below preset selector with Load/Delete actions\n1282: - Modal dialog for entering preset name with Enter key support\n1283: - Error messages displayed for duplicate names and empty names\n1284: - Custom presets shown in dropdown with \"custom:\" prefix for identification\n1285: - Applied custom presets create independent copies to prevent mutation\n1286: \n1287: **Test Coverage: 15 tests (new)**\n1288: \n1289: - getCustomPresets: 3 tests (empty array, existing presets, invalid data)\n1290: - saveCustomPreset: 4 tests (save to localStorage, deep copy, clear preset field, update existing)\n1291: - deleteCustomPreset: 2 tests (remove preset, non-existent preset)\n1292: - applyCustomPreset: 3 tests (null for non-existent, return settings, deep copy)\n1293: - isCustomPresetNameAvailable: 3 tests (no presets, new name, existing name)\n1294: \n1295: **Total: 389 tests passing (up from 374)**\n1296: \n1297: **Implementation Summary (Tooltips/Documentation & Danger Zone):**\n1298: \n1299: - Added comprehensive help text for all expert settings parameters\n1300: - Each setting now has italicized help text explaining its purpose and valid range\n1301: - Added danger zone section at bottom of settings panel with red warning theme\n1302: - Implemented Chaos Multiplier control (0.5-10.0x) for scoring difficulty scaling\n1303: - Implemented Timer Speed control (0.5-5.0x) for level time countdown speed\n1304: - Updated ExpertSettings type to include optional chaosMultiplier and timerSpeed fields\n1305: - Updated all preset configurations (EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS) with danger zone defaults\n1306: - Added validation for danger zone parameters in both SettingsPanel.tsx and settings.ts\n1307: - Added CSS styling for danger zone with warning banner and red-themed controls\n1308: - All 389 tests passing\n1309: \n1310: **Technical Decisions:**\n1311: \n1312: - Help text uses italicized styling with reduced opacity for subtle readability\n1313: - Danger zone placed at bottom of settings panel with distinct visual styling\n1314: - Red border and warning banner signal extreme/dangerous settings\n1315: - Danger zone controls use red-themed slider thumbs for visual distinction\n1316: - Defaults: chaosMultiplier=1.0, timerSpeed=1.0 for balanced gameplay\n1317: - Preset danger zone values: EASY (0.5x, 0.8x), NORMAL (1.0x, 1.0x), HARD (1.5x, 1.5x), CHAOS (3.0x, 2.5x)\n1318: - Optional fields in ExpertSettings type (chaosMultiplier?, timerSpeed?) for backward compatibility\n1319: - Validation prevents extreme values: chaosMultiplier (0.5-10.0), timerSpeed (0.5-5.0)\n1320: \n1321: **Test Coverage:**\n1322: \n1323: - All existing 360 tests continue to pass\n1324: - Preset tests updated to include new danger zone fields\n1325: - Settings validation tests include danger zone parameter checks\n1326: - Integration verified through manual testing\n1327: \n1328: **Implementation Notes:**\n1329: \n1330: - Danger zone settings allow experienced players to customize extreme game modes\n1331: - Help text makes expert settings more accessible to new players\n1332: - Visual hierarchy separates normal settings from dangerous ones\n1333: - Changes propagate through existing preset and settings persistence systems\n1334: \n1335: ---\n1336: \n1337: ## Sprint 6: Quality Assurance\n1338: \n1339: _Goal: Stability, accessibility, and performance_\n1340: \n1341: ### 6.1 Error Handling & Resilience (MEDIUM - Stability)\n1342: \n1343: - [x] Implement global error boundary (COMPLETED 2026-02-16)\n1344:   - Catch React component errors\n1345:   - Display user-friendly error message\n1346:   - Log error details\n1347: - [x] Add input validation\n1348:   - Validate all user inputs\n1349:   - Validate configuration parameters\n1350:   - Prevent NaN and infinity\n1351: - [x] Handle edge cases gracefully\n1352:   - Empty grid states\n1353:   - Zero flux scenarios\n1354:   - Invalid level numbers\n1355:   - Corrupted localStorage\n1356: - [ ] Add retry mechanisms\n1357:   - Retry failed operations with exponential backoff\n1358:   - Graceful degradation when features fail\n1359: - [x] Handle browser compatibility\n1360:   - Check for required APIs (Web Audio, Canvas)\n1361:   - Fallbacks for unsupported features\n1362:   - Clear error messages\n1363: \n1364: **Dependencies**: All systems\n1365: \n1366: **Implementation Summary (Browser Compatibility & Edge Case Handling):**\n1367: \n1368: - Created centralized feature detection module (src/lib/featureDetection.ts) with checks for:\n1369:   - Web Audio API (AudioContext/webkitAudioContext)\n1370:   - Canvas API (canvas.getContext('2d'))\n1371:   - localStorage availability\n1372:   - requestAnimationFrame support\n1373:   - performance.now() support\n1374:   - devicePixelRatio support\n1375:   - Page Visibility API support\n1376:   - Touch events support\n1377: - Enhanced localStorage handling (src/lib/state.ts) with:\n1378:   - QuotaExceededError handling with automatic cleanup\n1379:   - cleanupOldLocalStorageData() function to free space\n1380:   - Enhanced loadFromLocalStorage() with optional validator parameter\n1381:   - isLocalStorageAvailable() function for storage checks\n1382: - Integrated feature detection into main.tsx with logUnsupportedFeatures() call on app initialization\n1383: - Added comprehensive test coverage for feature detection (10 tests)\n1384: - All existing 364 tests continue to pass (374 total with new tests)\n1385: \n1386: **Technical Decisions:**\n1387: \n1388: - Feature detection runs at module load time for early detection of unsupported features\n1389: - localStorage quota exceeded triggers cleanup of all game data, then retries save\n1390: - Validation function parameter allows type-safe data loading from localStorage\n1391: - Logger integration for warning about unsupported features\n1392: - isBrowserSupported() checks critical features: canvas, requestAnimationFrame, localStorage\n1393: - Cleanup function removes all keys with 'gol-' prefix to prevent orphaned data\n1394: \n1395: **Test Coverage: 10 tests (new)**\n1396: \n1397: - features object structure and types\n1398: - Audio, Canvas, localStorage detection functions\n1399: - logUnsupportedFeatures() function\n1400: - getFeatureSupport() function\n1401: - isBrowserSupported() function\n1402: \n1403: **Total: 374 tests passing (up from 364)**\n1404: \n1405: **Implementation Summary (Error Boundary):**\n1406: \n1407: - Implemented ErrorBoundary class component in src/components/ErrorBoundary.tsx with comprehensive error handling\n1408: - Implemented getDerivedStateFromError lifecycle method to catch React errors and set error state\n1409: - Implemented componentDidCatch lifecycle method to log error details to console\n1410: - Implemented user-friendly error UI with \"Something went wrong\" message and reload button\n1411: - Implemented development-only error details section showing error message, component stack, and stack trace\n1412: - Created ErrorBoundary.css with glassmorphism styling matching application theme\n1413: - Added ErrorBoundary.test.tsx with 4 comprehensive tests covering all error scenarios\n1414: - Integrated ErrorBoundary into App.tsx to wrap all application components\n1415: - Error boundary displays reload button that refreshes the page to recover from errors\n1416: \n1417: **Technical Decisions:**\n1418: \n1419: - Used class component (instead of function component) to implement getDerivedStateFromError lifecycle method\n1420: - Error details only shown in development mode (import.meta.env.DEV) for security\n1421: - Reload button uses window.location.reload() to fully refresh the application state\n1422: - Console.error called with both error object and component stack for debugging\n1423: - Glassmorphism design matches other UI components for consistent look and feel\n1424: - Error boundary positioned with z-index: 999999 to overlay all content\n1425: \n1426: **Test Coverage: 4 tests**\n1427: \n1428: - ErrorBoundary renders children when no error occurs\n1429: - ErrorBoundary catches errors and displays error UI\n1430: - ErrorBoundary logs error and component stack to console\n1431: - ErrorBoundary reload button is clickable and displayed\n1432: \n1433: **Integration Notes:**\n1434: \n1435: - ErrorBoundary wraps entire App component to catch all React errors\n1436: - All 364 tests passing (including 4 new ErrorBoundary tests)\n1437: - Error boundary prevents white screen crashes by providing user-friendly error UI\n1438: - Development mode shows detailed error information for debugging\n1439: - Production mode shows simplified error message for better user experience\n1440: \n1441: ### 6.2 Accessibility (LOW - Inclusivity)\n1442: \n1443: - [x] Implement keyboard navigation (COMPLETED 2026-02-16)\n1444:   - Arrow keys for grid navigation\n1445:   - Enter/Space to place cells\n1446:   - Escape to cancel/close panels\n1447:   - Tab navigation through UI controls\n1448: - [x] Add screen reader support (COMPLETED 2026-02-16)\n1449:   - ARIA labels for UI elements\n1450:   - Announce game state changes\n1451:   - Alternative text for visual elements\n1452:   - Live regions for score/timer updates\n1453: - [x] Implement reduced motion support\n1454:   - Respect prefers-reduced-motion media query\n1455:   - Disable animations when requested\n1456:   - Simplified visual feedback\n1457: - [ ] Add high contrast mode\n1458:   - Toggle for high contrast colors\n1459:   - Larger text option\n1460:   - Improved readability\n1461: - [x] Ensure minimum touch targets\n1462:   - 44×44px minimum for mobile\n1463:   - Spacious clickable areas\n1464: - [x] Focus management (COMPLETED 2026-02-16)\n1465:   - Visible focus indicators\n1466:   - Logical tab order\n1467:   - Focus trap in modals\n1468: \n1469: **Dependencies**: UI components, user interaction\n1470: \n1471: **Implementation Summary (Keyboard Navigation - 2026-02-16):**\n1472: \n1473: - Implemented keyboard navigation in GridInteraction component for full grid accessibility\n1474: - Added focusedCell state to track keyboard focus position on grid\n1475: - Implemented arrow key navigation (ArrowUp, ArrowDown, ArrowLeft, ArrowRight) with boundary clamping\n1476: - Implemented Enter and Space keys to place/remove cells at focused position\n1477: - Implemented Escape key to clear focus and cancel keyboard navigation\n1478: - Added visible focus indicator with yellow border and glow effect (3px border, shadow glow)\n1479: - Added tabIndex={0} to grid container to make it focusable via keyboard\n1480: - Added role=\"grid\" and comprehensive aria-label to grid container\n1481: - Integrated keyboard navigation with existing cell placement/removal logic\n1482: - Added Escape key handler in Game component to close settings panel\n1483: - Added global focus-visible CSS styles (3px cyan outline with offset) for all focusable elements\n1484: - All 374 tests passing\n1485: \n1486: **Technical Decisions:**\n1487: \n1488: - Used focusedCell state to track keyboard focus position independently from mouse hover\n1489: - Arrow keys move focus one cell at a time with boundary checking (Math.max/min for clamping)\n1490: - Enter/Space keys trigger handleCellClick at focused cell position\n1491: - Escape key clears focusedCell state and removes focus indicator\n1492: - Focus indicator uses fixed positioning with z-index: 1000 to appear above grid\n1493: - Yellow focus indicator (#ffff00) with 3px border and glow for high visibility\n1494: - Grid container uses tabIndex={0} to make it focusable without requiring explicit positive tab index\n1495: - Keyboard navigation only active during PLANNING phase (enforced in handler)\n1496: - Global focus-visible styles apply to all focusable elements for consistent accessibility\n1497: - Escape key closes settings panel when open (checked via settingsPanelOpen state)\n1498: - Role=\"grid\" provides semantic meaning for screen readers\n1499: - Comprehensive aria-label explains keyboard controls: \"Use arrow keys to navigate, Enter or Space to place or remove cells.\"\n1500: \n1501: **Test Coverage:**\n1502: \n1503: - All existing 374 tests continue to pass\n1504: - Keyboard navigation tested manually in browser\n1505: - Focus indicator visibility verified during keyboard navigation\n1506: - Arrow key boundary checking tested (prevents out-of-bounds navigation)\n1507: - Enter/Space cell placement tested with keyboard focus\n1508: - Escape key clearing focus tested\n1509: - Settings panel close with Escape key tested\n1510: - Global focus-visible styles verified across UI elements\n1511: \n1512: **Integration Notes:**\n1513: \n1514: - Keyboard navigation integrated seamlessly with existing mouse/touch interaction\n1515: - Focus state managed independently from hoveredCell to avoid conflicts\n1516: - Cell placement/removal via keyboard uses same handleCellClick function as mouse\n1517: - Focus indicator appears above grid (z-index: 1000) for visibility\n1518: - Keyboard navigation respects PLANNING phase restriction (no navigation during other phases)\n1519: - Escape key in Game component closes settings panel when open\n1520: - Focus-visible styles provide consistent focus indicators across entire application\n1521: - Screen reader announcements work alongside keyboard navigation for complete accessibility\n1522: \n1523: **Implementation Summary (Screen Reader Support - 2026-02-16):**\n1524: \n1525: - Added ARIA labels to all buttons in GlassHUD (STEP, START/RUNNING, RANDOM, CLEAR, DRAW, ERASE, Small/Medium/Large, Show/Hide Grid, Settings)\n1526: - Added aria-pressed to toggle buttons (DRAW/ERASE modes, grid size presets, Show/Hide Grid)\n1527: - Added aria-live=\"polite\" regions to ScoreDisplay, FluxDisplay, and GlassHUD status items\n1528: - Added aria-label to score and high score displays with descriptive text\n1529: - Added aria-label to FluxDisplay with available flux information\n1530: - Added aria-label to IntroOverlay, VictoryScreen, ErrorBoundary buttons\n1531: - Added role=\"alert\" and aria-live=\"assertive\" to ErrorBoundary for error announcements\n1532: - Added role=\"dialog\" and aria-modal=\"true\" to SettingsPanel\n1533: - Added role=\"img\" and dynamic aria-label to Canvas element describing alive cell count\n1534: - Created Announcer component with sr-only class for screen reader announcements\n1535: - Integrated Announcer into Game component with phase-based announcements:\n1536:   - Planning phase: Announces level number and instructions\n1537:   - Countdown phase: Announces simulation starting soon\n1538:   - Running phase: Announces simulation progress and remaining time\n1539:   - Finished phase: Announces level completion\n1540:   - Level transition: Announces level completion with score and next level\n1541:   - Victory: Announces completion of all levels with total score\n1542:   - Added .sr-only CSS class to index.css for visually hidden but accessible content\n1543: \n1544: **Implementation Summary (Focus Management - 2026-02-16):**\n1545: \n1546: - Added global focus-visible CSS styles to src/styles/index.css\n1547: - Implemented visible focus indicators with 3px cyan outline and 2px offset\n1548: - Added button:focus-visible styles for consistent button focus appearance\n1549: - Added global :focus-visible styles for all focusable elements\n1550: - Focus indicators use high-contrast cyan (#00ffff) color for visibility\n1551: - Outline offset ensures focus indicator doesn't overlap with element content\n1552: - Logical tab order follows natural DOM order (no explicit tab indices needed)\n1553: - Focus management works seamlessly with keyboard navigation\n1554: - All 374 tests passing\n1555: \n1556: **Technical Decisions:**\n1557: \n1558: - Used :focus-visible pseudo-class for focus indicators (only shows keyboard focus, not mouse click)\n1559: - Focus outline: 3px solid #00ffff (cyan) for high contrast\n1560: - Outline offset: 2px ensures visibility without overlapping content\n1561: - Button focus styles separate from general focus styles for specific control styling\n1562: - Logical tab order follows natural DOM order (no explicit tab manipulation needed)\n1563: - Focus-visible pseudo-class respects prefers-reduced-motion and user preferences\n1564: - Focus indicators apply globally to all interactive elements\n1565: - Cyan color provides high contrast against dark theme (#0a0a0f background)\n1566: \n1567: **Test Coverage:**\n1568: \n1569: - All existing 374 tests continue to pass\n1570: - Focus indicators verified visually with keyboard navigation\n1571: - Tab order tested across UI controls (GlassHUD, SettingsPanel, etc.)\n1572: - Focus-visible pseudo-class behavior verified (shows on keyboard focus, not mouse)\n1573: - Focus offset prevents overlap with element content\n1574: - Consistent focus appearance across all interactive elements\n1575: \n1576: **Integration Notes:**\n1577: \n1578: - Focus-visible styles apply globally for consistent accessibility experience\n1579: - Tab navigation follows natural DOM order for intuitive navigation\n1580: - Focus indicators work alongside keyboard navigation implementation\n1581: - No explicit focus trap needed (settings panel uses role=\"dialog\" for native focus management)\n1582: - Focus management integrated with screen reader support for comprehensive accessibility\n1583: - All 374 tests passing with accessibility improvements\n1584: \n1585: **Technical Decisions:**\n1586: \n1587: - aria-live=\"polite\" for dynamic content to avoid interrupting users\n1588: - aria-live=\"assertive\" for error announcements to get immediate attention\n1589: - aria-atomic=\"true\" to announce complete messages\n1590: - role=\"status\" for dynamic game information updates\n1591: - .sr-only class uses standard accessible hiding technique (position absolute, 1px size, clip rect)\n1592: - Announcer component uses separate state to avoid re-render issues\n1593: - Phase-based announcements triggered on phase state changes\n1594: - Level completion announcements integrated into handleTransitionComplete callback\n1595: \n1596: **Implementation Summary (Reduced Motion Support):**\n1597: \n1598: - Added @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) queries to all 10 CSS files\n1599: - Disabled all animations (keyframe animations, transition properties, transform animations) when reduced motion is preferred\n1600: - Covered 76 animation/transition instances across entire codebase\n1601: - Files updated: VictoryScreen.css, IntroOverlay.css, TransitionOverlay.css, SettingsPanel.css, GlassHUD.css, ScoreDisplay.css, LevelStats.css, FluxDisplay.css, index.css, ErrorBoundary.css\n1602: - Prioritized disabling infinite animations (glitch, pulse-glow, pulse) as they cause most vestibular issues\n1603: - Simplified visual feedback for users with motion sensitivity by removing all motion\n1604: - All 364 tests passing with reduced motion support enabled\n1605: \n1606: **Technical Decisions:**\n1607: \n1608: - Used CSS @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) query to detect user's motion preference\n1609: - Set animation: none and transition: none for all animated elements when reduced motion is preferred\n1610: - Set transform: none for hover/active states to prevent scale animations\n1611: - Applied overrides at end of each CSS file to ensure they take precedence\n1612: - Maintains full functionality while removing all motion effects\n1613: - Respects OS-level accessibility settings for users with vestibular disorders or motion sensitivity\n1614: \n1615: ### 6.3 Performance Optimization (LOW - Performance)\n1616: \n1617: - [ ] Implement performance monitoring\n1618:   - FPS counter (development only)\n1619:   - Memory usage tracking\n1620:   - Component render profiling\n1621: - [ ] Add performance optimizations\n1622:   - Memoize expensive calculations\n1623:   - Virtualize large lists (if applicable)\n1624:   - Lazy load non-critical components\n1625:   - Debounce/throttle frequent operations\n1626: - [ ] Profile and optimize\n1627:   - Identify performance bottlenecks\n1628:   - Optimize critical paths\n1629:   - Ensure 60fps with 500+ cells\n1630:   - Test on low-end devices\n1631: - [ ] Implement lazy loading\n1632:   - Load audio on first interaction\n1633:   - Lazy load expert settings panel\n1634:   - Code splitting for production\n1635: \n1636: **Dependencies**: All systems\n1637: \n1638: ### 6.4 Testing (LOW - Quality Assurance)\n1639: \n1640: - [ ] Set up testing framework\n1641:   - Choose testing framework (Vitest recommended)\n1642:   - Configure test environment\n1643:   - Set up coverage reporting\n