{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771237848951,"sessionID":"ses_39a00e1f2ffeTfoOwyWI4Ya0up","part":{"id":"prt_c66005033001v9kjTpeTUv4TDY","sessionID":"ses_39a00e1f2ffeTfoOwyWI4Ya0up","messageID":"msg_c65ffaccc001Z1hKDiWgL1gW5p","type":"tool","callID":"call_b494e0c87f4941f5969513a9","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Study specs for movement & scoring","prompt":"Study these spec files and provide a comprehensive summary of all requirements, features, and technical details:\n\n1. /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/movement-detection.md\n2. /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/scoring-system.md\n\nFor each spec, identify:\n- Core functionality requirements\n- Technical implementation details\n- Edge cases and constraints\n- Dependencies on other systems\n- What's already implemented vs what's missing\n\nReturn a detailed summary of your findings.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_399ffafc1ffeRh87LY0Q5NXHqW (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n# Comprehensive Summary of Spec Files\n\n---\n\n## 1. Movement Detection Spec (`movement-detection.md`)\n\n### Core Functionality Requirements\n\n**Connected Component Detection**\n- Identify clusters of adjacent live cells using 8-connectivity (including diagonal neighbors)\n- Each cluster has: unique ID, set of cells (as \"x,y\" coordinate strings), centroid coordinates, and generation first identified\n- Function: `findConnectedComponents(grid: boolean[][]): CellCluster[]`\n\n**Centroid Tracking**\n- Track cluster centroids across generations to calculate velocity vectors\n- Maintain history of last N centroids (configurable, default: 5)\n- Store velocity vector (dx, dy) and classification for each tracked cluster\n- Classify clusters into three types: `MOVER`, `OSCILLATOR`, or `STATIC`\n\n**Classification Algorithm**\n1. Calculate centroid velocity by comparing current position to earliest history position\n2. Apply movement threshold (default: 0.5 cells) to classify:\n   - **MOVER**: `|dx| > threshold` OR `|dy| > threshold` (centroid translating)\n   - **OSCILLATOR**: Centroid static within threshold, but cell set changes (local movement)\n   - **STATIC**: Centroid static AND cell set unchanged\n3. Match clusters across generations using nearest centroid approach\n\n### Technical Implementation Details\n\n**Data Structures**\n```typescript\ninterface CellCluster {\n  id: string;                    // Unique identifier (hash of coordinates)\n  cells: Set<string>;             // \"x,y\" coordinate strings\n  centroid: { x: number; y: number };\n  generation: number;\n}\n\ninterface TrackedCluster extends CellCluster {\n  centroidHistory: { x: number; y: number }[];\n  velocity: { dx: number; dy: number };\n  classification: 'MOVER' | 'OSCILLATOR' | 'STATIC';\n}\n\ninterface TrackingConfig {\n  historyLength: number;        // Default: 5\n  movementThreshold: number;      // Default: 0.5 cells\n}\n```\n\n**Performance Requirements**\n- Run connected component analysis every generation during RUNNING phase\n- Must process in < 16ms for 60fps\n- Benchmark: 100×100 grid should expect 50-200 clusters maximum\n- Must scale with actual game grid sizes (20×30, 40×50, 60×80)\n\n**Optimizations**\n- Store cluster history in circular buffer for efficient memory usage\n- Use Manhattan or Euclidean distance for centroid matching\n- Only recompute centroids for changed regions, not full grid\n- Limit history buffer size to prevent unbounded memory growth\n\n**UI/UX Requirements**\n- Display \"active patterns\" count in HUD\n- Highlight moving patterns with subtle glow effect\n\n### Edge Cases and Constraints\n\n| Edge Case | Description | Handling Approach |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------------|\n| **Cluster Split** | One cluster becomes two (e.g., glider collision) | Track both as new clusters or attempt lineage |\n| **Cluster Merge** | Two clusters become one | Classification reset to avoid double-counting |\n| **Oscillator Periods** | Blinker (period 2), Pulsar (period 3) - cells swap but centroid unchanged | Detect cell set changes vs centroid position |\n| **Glider Guns** | Stationary structure producing moving gliders | Gun = STATIC, produced gliders = MOVERS |\n| **Minimum Cluster Size** | Single isolated cell | Decide: treat as cluster of size 1 or ignore |\n| **Large Grid Performance** | 100×100 grid with many clusters | Must maintain <16ms processing time |\n\n### Dependencies on Other Systems\n\n- **Grid System**: Requires access to current grid state (boolean[][])\n- **Game Loop**: Must run every generation during RUNNING phase\n- **Rendering System**: Needs to highlight moving patterns with glow effect\n- **Settings System**: Expert setting for `historyLength`\n\n---\n\n## 2. Scoring System Spec (`scoring-system.md`)\n\n### Core Functionality Requirements\n\n**Scoring Formula**\n- Points awarded per generation based on cluster classification\n- Movers earn: 10 points (range: 1-100)\n- Oscillators earn: 2 points (range: 0-20)\n- Static patterns earn: 0 points\n- All points multiplied by configurable multiplier (default: 1.0, range: 0.1-5.0)\n\n**Per-Generation Calculation**\n```typescript\nfunction calculateGenerationScore(\n  trackedClusters: TrackedCluster[],\n  config: ScoringConfig\n): number\n```\n- Sum points for all active clusters\n- Apply score multiplier\n- Add to cumulative score\n\n**Score Persistence**\n- Score resets to 0 at start of each level (no carry-over)\n- High score per level saved to localStorage for progress tracking\n\n### Technical Implementation Details\n\n**Data Structures**\n```typescript\ninterface ScoringConfig {\n  moverPointsPerGeneration: number;      // Default: 10, range: 1-100\n  oscillatorPointsPerGeneration: number;   // Default: 2, range: 0-20\n  staticPointsPerGeneration: number;     // Always 0\n  scoreMultiplier: number;                 // Default: 1.0, range: 0.1-5.0\n}\n\ninterface ScoreState {\n  currentScore: number;\n  generationScore: number;      // Points earned this generation\n  totalPatternsTracked: number; // Stats: total patterns ever detected\n}\n```\n\n**Performance & Implementation**\n- Scoring must be deterministic (same patterns = same score)\n- Calculate in separate thread or use `requestIdleCallback` if heavy\n- Decouple from render if tracking causes >16ms lag\n- Config stored in expert settings with defaults\n\n**UI/UX Requirements**\n\n**Score Display**\n- Location: Top-left of screen\n- Format: Large number with \"PTS\" label\n- Color: White/bright, stands out from grid\n- Animation: Smooth increment when score changes, brief pulse/flash on point gain\n\n**Pattern Breakdown (Optional)**\n- Active Movers: [count]\n- Active Oscillators: [count]\n- Current Rate: [points/gen]\n\n**End-of-Level Stats** (display on FINISHED phase)\n- Final Score: [number]\n- Time Survived: [seconds]\n- Patterns Created: [count]\n\n**Score Animation**\n- Real-time updates every generation during RUNNING phase\n- Smooth counting up effect (lerp over 0.2s)\n- Brief flash every 100 points (optional milestone)\n\n### Edge Cases and Constraints\n\n| Edge Case | Description | Handling Approach |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------------|\n| **Score Overflow** | Potential for very large scores | Cap at `MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` (9,007,199,254,740,991) |\n| **Negative Multiplier** | Could reduce score or make it negative | Expert settings validation must prevent negative values |\n| **Zero Points Generation** | No patterns active | UI must handle gracefully (no animation) |\n| **Score Calculation Lag** | Tracking takes >16ms, delays score update | Decouple scoring from render using separate thread or `requestIdleCallback` |\n\n### Dependencies on Other Systems\n\n- **Movement Detection System**: Requires `TrackedCluster[]` with classifications\n- **Game Loop**: Must calculate and update score every generation during RUNNING phase\n- **Rendering System**: Needs to display score with animations\n- **Settings System**: Scoring config stored as expert settings\n- **Storage System**: localStorage for high score persistence per level\n- **Phase Management**: Different displays for RUNNING vs FINISHED phases\n\n---\n\n## Cross-Spec Dependencies & Integration\n\nBoth specs are tightly coupled:\n\n1. **Scoring depends on Movement Detection**: The scoring system requires `TrackedCluster[]` with classifications from the movement detection system\n2. **Shared Performance Constraints**: Both must execute in <16ms to maintain 60fps\n3. **Expert Settings Integration**: Both have configurable parameters exposed through expert settings\n4. **Game Phase Awareness**: Both only operate during RUNNING phase\n5. **Shared Data Flow**: Grid → Connected Components → Tracked Clusters → Score Calculation → UI Display\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Status Assessment\n\n**Based on spec analysis, here's what needs to be built:**\n\n### Movement Detection - Not Implemented\n- ❌ Connected component detection algorithm\n- ❌ Centroid tracking with history buffer\n- ❌ Classification logic (MOVER/OSCILLATOR/STATIC)\n- ❌ Cluster split/merge handling\n- ❌ Performance optimizations (circular buffer, partial recomputation)\n- ❌ UI integration (pattern count, glow effects)\n\n### Scoring System - Not Implemented\n- ❌ Per-generation score calculation\n- ❌ Score state management\n- ❌ Animated score display\n- ❌ Optional pattern breakdown UI\n- ❌ End-of-level stats display\n- ❌ High score persistence to localStorage\n- ❌ Score multiplier configuration\n\n**Both specs represent new features that need to be implemented from scratch.**\n</task_result>","title":"Study specs for movement & scoring","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_399ffafc1ffeRh87LY0Q5NXHqW","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771237822524,"end":1771237848948}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771237881432,"sessionID":"ses_39a00e1f2ffeTfoOwyWI4Ya0up","part":{"id":"prt_c6600502a0015GzCDy2ThrymZl","sessionID":"ses_39a00e1f2ffeTfoOwyWI4Ya0up","messageID":"msg_c65ffaccc001Z1hKDiWgL1gW5p","type":"tool","callID":"call_6b3fbb70f1184fb9b1438600","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Study specs for audio & simulation","prompt":"Study these spec files and provide a comprehensive summary of all requirements, features, and technical details:\n\n1. /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/audio-sonification.md\n2. /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/simulation-engine.md\n\nFor each spec, identify:\n- Core functionality requirements\n- Technical implementation details\n- Edge cases and constraints\n- Dependencies on other systems\n- What's already implemented vs what's missing\n\nReturn a detailed summary of your findings.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_399ffafcdffe0JkjXCuY51Tq1y (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my analysis of both spec files and the codebase, here's a comprehensive summary:\n\n---\n\n# Spec Analysis Summary\n\n## 1. Audio Sonification System\n\n### Core Functionality Requirements\n\n**Specified:**\n- Real-time sound generation using Web Audio API\n- **Generation Sounds**: Triggered after each simulation step with births\n  - Pitch mapped to average row position of new births (higher rows = higher pitch)\n  - Intensity mapped to number of births\n  - Four waveform options: sine (default), triangle, square, sawtooth\n- **Interaction Sounds**: \n  - Draw sound: Higher pitch (~880Hz), short duration\n  - Erase sound: Lower pitch (~440Hz), short duration\n- **Volume Control**: Range 0.0-0.5, default 0.1\n- **Enable/Disable toggle**\n\n### Technical Implementation Details\n\n**Specified:**\n```typescript\ninterface SoundEngine {\n  setEnabled(enabled: boolean): void\n  setVolume(volume: number): void\n  setWaveform(waveform: OscillatorType): void\n  playGenerationSound(bornCount: number, avgRow: number, totalRows: number): void\n  playInteractionSound(type: 'draw' | 'erase'): void\n}\n```\n\n- Lazy AudioContext initialization (browser autoplay policy)\n- Envelope: Quick attack, exponential decay\n- Polyphonic (concurrent sounds allowed)\n- Frequency range: 880Hz (based on spec formula)\n\n### What's Already Implemented vs Spec\n\n**✅ Fully Implemented (matches spec):**\n- All required methods: `setEnabled`, `setVolume`, `setWaveform`, `playGenerationSound`, `playInteractionSound`\n- Lazy initialization with context resumption\n- Proper early returns for disabled state and no births\n- Volume and waveform parameter validation\n- Volume scaling with sqrt(bornCount)\n- Polyphonic sound generation\n\n**➕ Extra Features (beyond spec):**\n- `playLevelCompleteSound()` - Two-oscillator chord (523.25Hz + 659.25Hz)\n- `playLevelStartSound()` - Single tone at 440Hz\n- `playTransitionSound()` - Fade-out/fade-in sounds (300-400Hz)\n- `playSimulationStartSound()` - Start sound at 330Hz\n- `playFluxErrorSound()` - Error tone using sawtooth waveform\n- `getContextState()` - Helper to check AudioContext state\n\n**🔧 Implementation Differences:**\n- Spec specifies linear attack ramp; implementation uses linearRampToValueAtTime with 10ms attack\n- Spec mentions \"10ms steps\" for volume slider; implementation uses 0.01 step size\n- Additional error handling in all sound methods with try-catch blocks\n\n### Edge Cases and Constraints\n\n**All Specified Edge Cases Handled:**\n- No births → Sound not triggered ✓\n- Suspended context → Resumes on next interaction ✓\n- Volume = 0 → Sounds generated but at 0 gain ✓\n- Disabled → Early return without generating sounds ✓\n- Multiple events → Concurrent sounds allowed ✓\n\n**Browser Compatibility:**\n- Modern browsers supported (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge)\n- iOS requires user gesture ✓\n- Autoplay policy handled with lazy initialization ✓\n\n### Dependencies\n\n**Specified:**\n- Core simulation engine: Provides birth statistics (bornCount, avgRow)\n- User interaction system: Triggers draw/erase sounds\n- UI/overlay system: Volume, waveform, enabled settings\n\n**Actual Implementation:**\n- Simulation engine provides birth count and average row via `stepSimulation()`\n- `GridInteraction` component triggers interaction sounds\n- `SettingsPanel` provides UI controls for audio settings\n- `Game` component manages SoundEngine lifecycle and configuration\n\n---\n\n## 2. Core Simulation Engine\n\n### Core Functionality Requirements\n\n**Specified:**\n- Conway's Game of Life rules: `born=[3]`, `survive=[2,3]`\n- Grid computation using Moore neighborhood (8 adjacent cells)\n- Toroidal boundary conditions (wraps edges)\n- Age tracking for cells (alive cells increment age each generation)\n- Speed control: 10ms to 500ms between steps\n- Running state management\n\n### Technical Implementation Details\n\n**Specified:**\n```typescript\ntype GridType = number[][] // Age-based cell storage\n\ninterface SimulationState {\n  grid: GridType\n  generation: number\n  running: boolean\n  speed: number\n  selectedRule: RuleSet\n}\n```\n\n- Double buffer pattern with deep copy\n- Precomputed neighbor offset array for performance\n- React ref for direct grid access (avoid render cycles)\n- Generation counter to trigger React renders\n\n**Audio Integration:**\n- Birth events tracked: count and row position\n- Average row position passed to sound engine for pitch mapping\n\n### What's Already Implemented vs Spec\n\n**✅ Fully Implemented (matches spec):**\n- All core functions: `createGrid`, `countNeighbors`, `applyRules`, `stepSimulation`\n- Toroidal boundary handling with modulo arithmetic\n- Age tracking (surviving cells increment age, new cells start at age 1)\n- Precomputed neighbor offsets\n- Conway rules constant\n- Grid presets (SMALL, MEDIUM, LARGE)\n\n**➕ Extra Features (beyond spec):**\n- `setCell()` - Update individual cell state\n- `clearGrid()` - Clear all cells\n- `randomFill()` - Fill grid with random cells (15% density)\n- `countAliveCells()` - Count total alive cells\n- `isGridEmpty()` - Check if grid has any alive cells\n- Grid size presets (20×30, 40×50, 60×80)\n\n**🔧 Implementation Differences:**\n- Spec mentions \"uses React ref\" for performance; implementation uses pure functions instead\n- Spec shows speed control at engine level; implementation in `Game` component uses setInterval\n- Spec shows `running` boolean in state; engine is stateless, managed by Game component\n\n### Edge Cases and Constraints\n\n**All Specified Edge Cases Handled:**\n- Empty grid → Simulation continues running with no births ✓\n- Static patterns (still lifes) → Survive indefinitely (e.g., block, beehive) ✓\n- Grid resizing → Clears history and resets when dimensions change ✓\n- Rapid speed changes → Speed ref updated immediately, no queue ✓\n\n**Additional Edge Cases Covered:**\n- Born cells start at age 1 ✓\n- Dead cells have value 0 ✓\n- Average row calculation handles division by zero (returns 0 when no births) ✓\n\n### Dependencies\n\n**Specified:**\n- Canvas rendering system: Receives grid state for visualization\n- Audio sonification system: Receives birth statistics\n- User interaction system: Modifies grid directly via ref\n\n**Actual Implementation:**\n- `CanvasGrid` component renders grid state\n- `SoundEngine.playGenerationSound()` receives bornCount and avgRow\n- `Game` component and `GridInteraction` modify grid via state\n\n---\n\n## Gap Analysis\n\n### Missing from Spec but Implemented:\n1. **Additional Sound Methods** (5 extra sound types for game events)\n2. **Utility Functions** (setCell, clearGrid, randomFill, countAliveCells, isGridEmpty)\n3. **Grid Size Presets** (SMALL/MEDIUM/LARGE configurations)\n4. **Helper Functions** (createInitialAudioParams, validateAudioParams)\n5. **AudioContext State Getter** (getContextState)\n\n### Specified but Missing from Code:\n1. **React ref pattern for grid access** - Implementation uses pure functions instead\n2. **Speed control at engine level** - Speed is managed at Game component level\n\n### Testing Coverage:\n- **Audio**: Well tested with mocks (disabled state, bornCount=0, parameter validation)\n- **Simulation**: Comprehensive tests for:\n  - Grid creation and manipulation\n  - Toroidal boundary handling\n  - Conway rules (block pattern, glider pattern)\n  - Age tracking\n  - Neighbor counting\n  - Grid presets\n\n### Architecture Notes:\n1. **SoundEngine** is implemented as a class with private methods\n2. **Simulation functions** are pure functions (no class)\n3. **Game component** acts as the orchestrator, managing SoundEngine lifecycle and simulation loop\n4. **SettingsPanel** provides comprehensive UI for all audio and simulation parameters\n\nBoth specs are largely well-implemented, with the audio system having more feature additions beyond the specification to support the game's level system and additional interactions.\n</task_result>","title":"Study specs for audio & simulation","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_399ffafcdffe0JkjXCuY51Tq1y","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771237822511,"end":1771237881427}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771237891185,"sessionID":"ses_39a00e1f2ffeTfoOwyWI4Ya0up","part":{"id":"prt_c66005044001FzZacgFRsUe1Cr","sessionID":"ses_39a00e1f2ffeTfoOwyWI4Ya0up","messageID":"msg_c65ffaccc001Z1hKDiWgL1gW5p","type":"tool","callID":"call_c38faf5a7ea84c52a1f6cb3a","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Study specs for phase & transitions","prompt":"Study these spec files and provide a comprehensive summary of all requirements, features, and technical details:\n\n1. /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/phase-management.md\n2. /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/auto-advance-transitions.md\n\nFor each spec, identify:\n- Core functionality requirements\n- Technical implementation details\n- Edge cases and constraints\n- Dependencies on other systems\n- What's already implemented vs what's missing\n\nReturn a detailed summary of your findings.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_399ffafafffenvGHdyznPd38bF (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n# Comprehensive Summary of Game Specifications\n\n---\n\n## 1. SPEC: Phase Management (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/phase-management.md`)\n\n### Core Functionality Requirements\n\n#### Phase Definitions\n- **PLANNING Phase**\n  - Entry: Level initialization or restart\n  - Duration: Unlimited (player-controlled)\n  - Allowed Actions: Place/remove cells using Flux\n  - UI: START button enabled when ≥1 cell placed\n  - Exit: Player clicks START button\n\n- **COUNTDOWN Phase**\n  - Entry: After START button clicked\n  - Duration: 3, 2, 1 countdown\n  - Allowed Actions: None (input blocked)\n  - UI: Large countdown display, \"Simulation starting\" sound\n  - Exit: Countdown completes → RUNNING\n\n- **RUNNING Phase**\n  - Entry: Countdown completes\n  - Duration: Level-specific (base 45s)\n  - Allowed Actions: Cell placement using saved Flux (add-only)\n  - Simulation: Game of Life rules execute automatically\n  - Exit: Timer reaches 0 OR all cells die → FINISHED\n\n- **FINISHED Phase**\n  - Entry: Timer expires or all cells die\n  - Duration: 2.0s pause before auto-advance\n  - Allowed Actions: None (view-only)\n  - UI: Score display, \"Time's Up\"/\"Level Complete\"\n  - Exit: Auto-advance after 2.0s\n\n#### State Machine\n```typescript\ntype GamePhase = 'PLANNING' | 'COUNTDOWN' | 'RUNNING' | 'FINISHED';\n\ninterface PhaseState {\n  current: GamePhase;\n  canTransition: boolean;\n  blockers: string[];\n}\n\nconst transitions = {\n  'PLANNING': ['COUNTDOWN'],\n  'COUNTDOWN': ['RUNNING'],\n  'RUNNING': ['FINISHED'],\n  'FINISHED': ['PLANNING'] // Circular to next level\n};\n```\n\n### Technical Implementation Details\n\n#### UI/UX Requirements\n- **PLANNING**: \"Place your cells\" text, START button (enabled ≥1 cell), Flux counter\n- **COUNTDOWN**: Large \"3... 2... 1...\" display, no input, simulation NOT running\n- **RUNNING**: Timer countdown, \"Simulation Running\" indicator, score ticking, Flux counter\n- **FINISHED**: Final score, cells alive, brief stats, auto-advance countdown\n\n#### Phase Transitions\n- PLANNING → COUNTDOWN: Immediate on START click\n- COUNTDOWN → RUNNING: After 3-2-1 completes, simulation starts\n- RUNNING → FINISHED: Timer 0 OR all cells die, simulation stops\n- FINISHED → PLANNING (next level): Fade out/in, fresh grid, no carryover\n\n#### Implementation Approach\n- React useReducer for phase state management\n- Guarded phase transitions (can't skip phases)\n- Accurate timing using `Date.now()` or `performance.now()`\n- Log phase transitions for debugging\n- Consider XState library if complexity grows\n\n### Edge Cases and Constraints\n\n1. **Zero Cells at Start**: START button disabled until ≥1 cell placed\n2. **All Cells Die Early**: Level ends immediately, score stops, auto-advance\n3. **Browser Tab Switch**: Timer continues running when tab inactive\n4. **Rapid Phase Switching**: Prevent multiple START clicks\n5. **Countdown Interrupted**: No input allowed during countdown\n6. **Level Transition**: No simulation carryover between levels - fresh start each level\n\n### Dependencies on Other Systems\n- Flux system for cell placement/removal\n- Scoring system for score accumulation\n- Audio system for phase transition sounds\n- Level system for level-specific time limits\n- Simulation system for Game of Life rules\n\n### What's Already Implemented\n- ✅ Phase state management (`/src/lib/phase.ts`)\n- ✅ Phase reducer with all actions\n- ✅ canTransition validation\n- ✅ getBlockers validation\n- ✅ usePhaseTimer hook (`/src/hooks/usePhaseTimer.ts`)\n- ✅ Full test coverage for phase logic (236 test lines)\n- ✅ Integration in Game.tsx\n- ✅ Phase display in GlassHUD\n- ✅ Announcer integration\n\n### What's Missing\n- ⚠️ Phase-specific sound effects partially implemented\n- ⚠️ Phase transition logging not verified\n- ⚠️ No explicit \"Simulation starting\" sound countdown hook\n\n---\n\n## 2. SPEC: Auto-Advance Transitions (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/auto-advance-transitions.md`)\n\n### Core Functionality Requirements\n\n#### Transition Trigger Configuration\n```typescript\ninterface TransitionConfig {\n  fadeOutDuration: number;        // Default: 2.0s\n  fadeInDuration: number;         // Default: 2.0s\n  interstitialDuration: number;   // Default: 2.0s\n  autoAdvanceDelay: number;       // Default: 2.0s\n  skipEnabled: boolean;            // Allow Space/ESC skip\n}\n```\n\n#### Transition States\n```typescript\ntype TransitionState = \n  | 'PLAYING'           // Normal gameplay\n  | 'FADING_OUT'        // Fade to black (opacity 0→1)\n  | 'INTERSTITIAL'      // Black screen, level info\n  | 'FADING_IN'         // Fade from black (opacity 1→0)\n  | 'READY';            // Next level loaded, waiting\n```\n\n#### Transition Sequence (Success)\n1. **FINISHED Display** (2.0s): Final score, \"Level Complete\", simulation rendering only (no scoring), SKIP available\n2. **Fade Out** (2.0s): Black overlay 0→1, ease-in-out, simulation hidden, SKIP available\n3. **Interstitial** (2.0s): Black screen, \"Level X Complete\" fading out, \"Level X+1\" fading in, load next level, reset state, SKIP available\n4. **Fade In** (2.0s): Black overlay 1→0, new level visible, simulation stopped, PLANNING ready, SKIP available\n5. **READY**: Player can immediately start placing cells\n\n#### Transition Sequence (Failure)\n- Similar fade to \"Game Over\" screen\n- \"Retry Level\" or \"Return to Menu\" options\n- No auto-advance (wait for input)\n\n### Technical Implementation Details\n\n#### UI/UX Requirements\n- **Fade Overlay**: Fixed position div, black (#000000), z-index above all, pointer-events none\n- **Interstitial Display**: Large centered text with fade animations\n- **Skip Indicator**: \"Press Space or ESC to skip\" at bottom\n- **Audio**: Fade volume during transitions (not abrupt cut)\n- **Visual Effects**: Optional blur, optional progress bar\n\n#### Implementation Approach\n- CSS transitions for smooth 60fps fades\n- React state machine for transition phases\n- Preload next level assets during fade-out\n- Mobile: Support `prefers-reduced-motion` (accessibility)\n- Skip transitions configurable in Expert Settings\n\n### Edge Cases and Constraints\n\n1. **Browser Tab During Transition**: Pause transition timer (unlike gameplay timer), resume on activation\n2. **Rapid Success**: Skip mechanism prevents tedium, allow holding Space/ESC to skip all\n3. **Last Level**: Fade to \"Victory\" screen with total score, \"Play Again\" or \"Return to Level 1\"\n4. **Interruption**: Space/ESC skips to end (READY state) at any point\n5. **Performance**: Use CSS `will-change: opacity`, consider reducing complexity for low-end devices\n6. **Browser Zoom**: Test all zoom levels to ensure full coverage\n\n### Dependencies on Other Systems\n- Phase system (FINISHED phase triggers transition)\n- Level system (load next level config)\n- Scoring system (display final stats)\n- Audio system (fade effects, transition sounds)\n- State management (reset Flux, Score, Grid)\n\n### What's Already Implemented\n- ✅ Transition state machine (`/src/hooks/useTransition.ts`)\n- ✅ All 5 transition states (PLAYING, FADING_OUT, INTERSTITIAL, FADING_IN, READY)\n- ✅ Skip functionality (Space/ESC)\n- ✅ Tab visibility handling (pause/resume transitions)\n- ✅ TransitionOverlay component (`/src/components/TransitionOverlay.tsx`)\n- ✅ CSS animations with ease-in-out easing\n- ✅ Accessibility: `prefers-reduced-motion` support\n- ✅ Full test coverage (136 test lines)\n- ✅ Audio integration (fade-out/fade-in callbacks)\n- ✅ Skip hint display\n- ✅ Level stats display during interstitial\n- ✅ Integration in Game.tsx with handleTransitionComplete\n- ✅ Victory screen for final level\n\n### What's Missing\n- ⚠️ Holding Space/ESC to skip all transitions (currently only single press)\n- ⚠️ Progress bar showing \"X of Y levels\" (optional, not critical)\n- ⚠️ Blur effect on game during fade (optional polish)\n- ⚠️ Level failure/Game Over transition sequence\n- ⚠️ \"Retry Level\" or \"Return to Menu\" options on failure\n- ⚠️ Audio volume fading during transitions (currently plays sounds but not verified fade)\n- ⚠️ Preload next level assets during fade-out (potential performance improvement)\n\n---\n\n## Cross-Spec Integration Notes\n\n### Phase & Transition Interaction\n1. Phase FINISHED triggers auto-transition after 2.0s delay\n2. Transitions handle level progression circularly (FINISHED → PLANNING of next level)\n3. Phase state and transition state run in parallel\n4. Victory screen handles final level (not transition)\n\n### Shared Edge Cases\n1. **Tab Visibility**: Different behavior for transitions (pause) vs gameplay (continue)\n2. **Timer Accuracy**: Both use Date.now() or performance.now() for accuracy\n3. **Skip/Rapid Action**: Both need guards against rapid user input\n\n### State Reset Requirements\n- ✅ Grid: Fresh empty grid each level\n- ✅ Flux: Reset to level's initialFlux\n- ✅ Score: Reset to 0 each level\n- ✅ Generation: Reset to 0 each level\n- ✅ TrackedClusters: Clear each level\n\n---\n\n## Overall Implementation Status\n\n### Core Functionality: **95% Complete**\nBoth spec requirements are largely implemented with:\n- Full state machines for phases and transitions\n- Comprehensive test coverage\n- Integration in main Game component\n- Visual components and CSS animations\n- Accessibility considerations\n\n### Minor Gaps to Address:\n1. Sound effects enhancement (phase-specific transition sounds)\n2. Failure/Game Over transition sequence\n3. Performance optimization (asset preloading)\n4. Optional polish features (blur, progress bar)\n\n### Architecture Strengths:\n- Clean separation of concerns (lib vs hooks vs components)\n- Well-tested core logic\n- Type-safe state management\n- Configurable via Expert Settings\n\nThe system is production-ready with minor enhancements possible for better UX and performance.\n</task_result>","title":"Study specs for phase & transitions","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_399ffafafffenvGHdyznPd38bF","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771237822542,"end":1771237891183}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771237910237,"sessionID":"ses_39a00e1f2ffeTfoOwyWI4Ya0up","part":{"id":"prt_c66005081001FLcYTPWd3g5Cdm","sessionID":"ses_39a00e1f2ffeTfoOwyWI4Ya0up","messageID":"msg_c65ffaccc001Z1hKDiWgL1gW5p","type":"tool","callID":"call_360959468eaa4c81866e87fd","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Study specs for UI & accessibility","prompt":"Study these spec files and provide a comprehensive summary of all requirements, features, and technical details:\n\n1. /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/ui-overlay.md\n2. /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/expert-settings.md\n3. /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/level-progression.md\n\nFor each spec, identify:\n- Core functionality requirements\n- Technical implementation details\n- Edge cases and constraints\n- Dependencies on other systems\n- What's already implemented vs what's missing\n\nReturn a detailed summary of your findings.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_399ffaf6cffexirekfMQaldpto (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nNow I have a comprehensive understanding of the specs and the current implementation. Let me provide you with a detailed summary.\n\n---\n\n# Comprehensive Spec Summary\n\n## 1. UI/Overlay System\n\n### Core Functionality Requirements\n\n**Cinematic Intro Overlay:**\n- Shows on app load with \"CONWAY'S GAME OF LIFE\" title and glitch effect\n- \"ENTER VOID\" CTA button triggers 1.2s exit animation\n- Game renders in background during intro\n- UI controls hidden until intro completes\n\n**Main Controls (Glass HUD):**\n- Semi-transparent glass container at bottom of screen\n- **Main Control Buttons:**\n  - PLAY/PAUSE: Toggle simulation\n  - STEP: Execute single generation (disabled while running)\n  - RANDOM: Fill grid at 15% cell density\n  - CLEAR: Remove all cells, reset generation (red text)\n- **Interaction Mode Buttons:**\n  - DRAW: Enable cell placement mode\n  - ERASE: Enable cell removal mode\n- **Status Controls:**\n  - Waveform selector (Sine, Triangle, Square, Saw)\n  - Volume slider (0-0.5, 0.01 step)\n  - Generation counter display\n  - Settings toggle (gear icon)\n\n**Phase Status Display:**\n- Always visible\n- Shows current phase: PLANNING, COUNTDOWN, RUNNING, FINISHED\n- Timer display during COUNTDOWN and RUNNING\n- Flux counter during PLANNING and RUNNING\n\n**Settings Panel:**\n- Access via gear icon in HUD\n- Speed slider (10ms-500ms)\n- Grid size buttons: Small (20×30), Medium (40×50), Large (60×80)\n- Show grid lines checkbox\n- Enable sonification checkbox\n- Expert Settings access button\n- Close button in header\n\n**UI Toggle:**\n- Icon frame in corner to show/hide all UI\n- Hidden when `enableUI` prop is false (intro mode)\n\n### Technical Implementation Details\n\n**State Management:**\n```typescript\ninterface UIState {\n  isUiVisible: boolean;        // Master visibility toggle\n  isIntro: boolean;            // Intro overlay active\n  isExiting: boolean;          // Intro exit animation\n  showSettings: boolean;       // Settings panel open\n  enableUI: boolean;           // Prop from App (false during intro)\n}\n```\n\n**CSS Architecture:**\n- Glass effect using `backdrop-filter: blur(10px)` with rgba backgrounds\n- Button states: Active (highlighted), Disabled (opacity reduced), Hover (brightness increase)\n- Animations: Intro exit (1.2s), panel slide-in, button hover transitions\n\n### Edge Cases and Constraints\n\n1. **Intro Exit**: Wait 1.2s for animation before removing component\n2. **UI Hidden**: All controls invisible, but toggle button remains accessible\n3. **Settings During Run**: Apply immediately without pause required\n4. **Grid Size Change**: Resets simulation\n5. **Clear Grid**: Removes all cells, resets generation counter\n\n### Dependencies on Other Systems\n\n- Core simulation: Speed and size settings affect simulation\n- Audio system: Enable toggle controls sonification\n- Canvas rendering: Grid line option affects rendering\n- User interaction: Mode buttons select draw/erase behavior\n- Phase management: Phase display shows current game state\n\n### Implementation Status: **FULLY IMPLEMENTED**\n\n| Component | Status |\n|-----------|--------|\n| IntroOverlay | ✅ Complete - /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/IntroOverlay.tsx |\n| GlassHUD | ✅ Complete - /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.tsx |\n| SettingsPanel | ✅ Complete - /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx |\n| UIToggleButton | ✅ Complete - /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/UIToggleButton.tsx |\n| Phase Status | ✅ Complete - integrated in GlassHUD |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Expert Settings / Dev Panel\n\n### Core Functionality Requirements\n\n**Access Methods:**\n- Keyboard shortcut: '`' (backtick) for quick access\n- Menu path: \"Settings → Advanced → Expert Mode\"\n- Mobile gesture: Triple-tap top-left corner\n\n**Configurable Parameters:**\n\n**Movement Detection:**\n- `centroidHistoryLength`: 3-10 generations (default: 5)\n- `movementThreshold`: 0.1-2.0 cells (default: 0.5)\n- `minClusterSize`: 1-5 cells (default: 1)\n\n**Scoring:**\n- `moverPointsPerGeneration`: 1-100 points (default: 10)\n- `oscillatorPointsPerGeneration`: 0-20 points (default: 2)\n- `scoreMultiplier`: 0.1-5.0x (default: 1.0)\n\n**Level Generation:**\n- `baseTimeSeconds`: 10-120s (default: 45)\n- `timeIncrementPerLevel`: 0-60s (default: 15)\n- `baseFlux`: 5-50 (default: 20)\n- `difficultyScalingMode`: TIME_ONLY, RESOURCE_ONLY, MIXED, EXTREME\n\n**Grid Sizing:**\n- `mobileCellSize`: 14-24px (default: 18)\n- `desktopCellSize`: 16-28px (default: 20)\n- `minVisibleCells`: minimum visible cells (default: 10)\n\n**Settings Persistence:**\n- Save to localStorage key `gol-expert-settings`\n- Load on app startup\n- \"Reset to Defaults\" button with confirmation\n- Export/Import settings as JSON\n\n### Technical Implementation Details\n\n**Data Structures:**\n- All parameters use TypeScript interfaces with validation\n- Schema validation using custom validators in `validateExpertSettings()`\n- Presets system: EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS (plus custom presets)\n- React state management with local state before saving\n\n**UI/UX Requirements:**\n- Modal overlay, centered or right sidebar\n- Collapsible sections by category\n- Sliders for numeric ranges, dropdowns for modes\n- Real-time updates with immediate application\n- Visual indicator when value differs from default\n- \"Revert\" button per section\n- Tooltips explaining each parameter\n\n**Danger Zone:**\n- Separate section for \"Break Things\" settings\n- Chaos multiplier: 0.5-10.0x\n- Timer speed: 0.5-5.0x\n- High contrast mode toggle\n- Confirmation required for extreme values\n\n### Edge Cases and Constraints\n\n1. **Invalid Values**: Input validation prevents negatives and out-of-range values\n2. **Settings While Running**: Scoring changes apply immediately; level changes on next level\n3. **Reset During Game**: Warn if game in progress before resetting\n4. **Corrupted Storage**: Fall back to defaults if localStorage has invalid JSON\n5. **Mobile Access**: Gesture detection must not conflict with game controls\n\n### Dependencies on Other Systems\n\n- Movement detection system: Uses detection parameters for pattern classification\n- Scoring system: Uses scoring parameters for point calculation\n- Level progression: Uses level generation parameters for difficulty scaling\n- Canvas rendering: Uses grid sizing parameters for cell dimensions\n- Phase management: Timer speed affects countdown duration\n\n### Implementation Status: **FULLY IMPLEMENTED**\n\n| Feature | Status |\n|---------|--------|\n| All parameter controls | ✅ Complete in SettingsPanel.tsx |\n| Preset system | ✅ Complete - /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/presets.ts |\n| Custom presets | ✅ Complete - save/load/delete implemented |\n| Export/Import JSON | ✅ Complete |\n| Validation | ✅ Complete - comprehensive validation in validateExpertSettingsDetailed() |\n| Persistence | ✅ Complete - localStorage integration |\n| Danger Zone | ✅ Complete - chaosMultiplier, timerSpeed, highContrastMode |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Level Progression\n\n### Core Functionality Requirements\n\n**Level Configuration:**\n```typescript\ninterface LevelConfig {\n  levelNumber: number;\n  timeLimitSeconds: number;\n  initialFlux: number;\n}\n\ninterface LevelProgression {\n  currentLevel: number;\n  maxUnlockedLevel: number;\n  totalScore: number;\n  levels: LevelConfig[];\n}\n```\n\n**Difficulty Scaling:**\nDefault strategy: Increase time for difficulty\n- Default generation: `timeLimitSeconds = 45 + (levelNum - 1) * 15`, `initialFlux = 20`\n- **TIME_ONLY**: Increase time, constant Flux\n- **RESOURCE_ONLY**: Constant time, decrease Flux\n- **MIXED**: Both time and Flux adjusted\n- **EXTREME**: Increase time slightly but aggressively reduce Flux\n\n**Progression Flow:**\n1. Player completes level N (timer reaches 0 or all cells die)\n2. Screen fades out over 2.0s\n3. Loading/interstitial (2.0s)\n4. Screen fades in to level N+1 with fresh grid\n5. Reset to PLANNING phase with fresh Flux\n6. Score accumulated across all levels\n\n**Game Objective:**\n- Maximize points within time limit and Flux budget\n- Level completion: Timer reaches 0 OR all cells die\n- No lose condition - game always advances\n- Total score displayed at end\n\n### Technical Implementation Details\n\n**Level Generation:**\n- Dynamic generation based on expert settings\n- Four difficulty scaling modes implemented\n- Default total levels: 10 (configurable)\n- High score tracking per level\n\n**Transition System:**\n- Fade out: 2.0s ease-out to black\n- Interstitial: Level number display (2.0s)\n- Fade in: 2.0s ease-in from black\n- Sound effects for transitions\n- Skip capability with Space/ESC\n\n**End Game:**\n- After final level, show victory screen\n- Display total accumulated score\n- Option to restart from level 1 or return to menu\n\n### Edge Cases and Constraints\n\n1. **Level 0 or Invalid**: Default to level 1 if undefined\n2. **Last Level**: Show victory screen with total score\n3. **Browser Refresh**: Optional persistence (not specified as required)\n4. **All Cells Die Early**: Level ends immediately, score stops, game advances\n\n### Dependencies on Other Systems\n\n- Scoring system: Calculates points for each level\n- Phase management: Controls level transitions\n- Timer system: Tracks time remaining per level\n- Flux system: Resets Flux budget each level\n- UI/Overlay: Displays level info, transitions, victory screen\n- Expert settings: Controls difficulty scaling parameters\n\n### Implementation Status: **FULLY IMPLEMENTED**\n\n| Feature | Status |\n|---------|--------|\n| Level generation | ✅ Complete - /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/level.ts |\n| Difficulty scaling modes | ✅ Complete - All 4 modes implemented |\n| Transition system | ✅ Complete - TransitionOverlay.tsx component |\n| Victory screen | ✅ Complete - VictoryScreen.tsx component |\n| High score tracking | ✅ Complete - saveHighScore(), getHighScore() functions |\n| Level progression flow | ✅ Complete - advanceLevel(), isFinalLevel() functions |\n| Level stats display | ✅ Complete - LevelStats.tsx component |\n\n---\n\n## Overall Implementation Assessment\n\n### What's Fully Implemented:\n\n1. **Complete UI System**: All overlays, HUD, settings panel, toggle button\n2. **Complete Expert Settings**: All parameters configurable with presets and validation\n3. **Complete Level Progression**: Generation, transitions, scoring, high scores\n4. **Persistence System**: localStorage for settings and high scores\n5. **Accessibility**: ARIA labels, keyboard navigation, high contrast mode\n6. **Responsive Design**: Mobile and desktop considerations\n\n### What May Need Attention:\n\n1. **Mobile gesture detection**: Triple-tap gesture for expert settings access (useTripleTapGesture hook exists but integration unclear)\n2. **Keyboard shortcut for expert settings**: Backtick shortcut may need implementation\n3. **Browser refresh persistence**: Level progress persistence is optional per spec\n4. **Audio transition sounds**: Not explicitly seen in implementation (may be handled by audio system)\n\n### Technical Architecture Strengths:\n\n- Clean component hierarchy with clear separation of concerns\n- Comprehensive TypeScript typing\n- Robust validation and error handling\n- Modular libraries for state, settings, levels, scoring\n- Test coverage exists for most components and utilities\n- CSS architecture supports glass effects, animations, responsive design\n\nThe implementation aligns very closely with all three specs, with all major features fully realized. The codebase is well-structured and maintainable, with proper abstractions for extensibility.\n</task_result>","title":"Study specs for UI & accessibility","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_399ffaf6cffexirekfMQaldpto","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771237822609,"end":1771237910234}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771237916463,"sessionID":"ses_39a00e1f2ffeTfoOwyWI4Ya0up","part":{"id":"prt_c66005069001reju6FvYtg1WsO","sessionID":"ses_39a00e1f2ffeTfoOwyWI4Ya0up","messageID":"msg_c65ffaccc001Z1hKDiWgL1gW5p","type":"tool","callID":"call_06f19c71a25643b4a098c5cf","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Study specs for rendering & grid","prompt":"Study these spec files and provide a comprehensive summary of all requirements, features, and technical details:\n\n1. /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/canvas-rendering.md\n2. /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/grid-interaction.md\n\nFor each spec, identify:\n- Core functionality requirements\n- Technical implementation details\n- Edge cases and constraints\n- Dependencies on other systems\n- What's already implemented vs what's missing\n\nReturn a detailed summary of your findings.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_399ffaf83ffe5jq3mzSOofIyIY (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nNow I have a complete picture. Let me provide a comprehensive summary of both spec files:\n\n---\n\n# COMPREHENSIVE SPEC SUMMARY\n\n## 1. Canvas Rendering System (`specs/canvas-rendering.md`)\n\n### Core Functionality Requirements\n\n**Theme & Visual Style:**\n- Dark neon theme with background color `#0a0a0f` (very dark blue-black)\n- Grid lines color: `#1a1a2e` (subtle)\n- Age-based cell colors with corresponding glow effects:\n  - Age 0 (just born): `#00ffff` (bright cyan), 15px shadow blur\n  - Age 1-2: `#61dafb` (React blue), 8px shadow blur\n  - Age 3-5: `#ff00ff` (magenta/pink), 4px shadow blur\n  - Age 6+: `#4a00ff` (deep purple), 2px shadow blur\n\n**Grid Rendering:**\n- Toggleable grid lines (G key shortcut)\n- Grid lines only visible during PLANNING phase\n- 1px stroke width\n- Grid lines drawn around each cell\n\n**Cell Rendering:**\n- Square cells with 2px corner radius\n- Responsive sizing: 18px mobile (<768px), 20px desktop (>=768px)\n- Glow effects applied via shadow blur matching cell color\n- Age-based color computation from cell state\n\n**Intensity Metric:**\n- CSS variable `--life-intensity` updated per frame\n- Scaled from 0-1 based on active cell count (0-500 cells)\n\n### Technical Implementation Details\n\n**Canvas Configuration:**\n```typescript\ninterface CanvasConfig {\n  width: number;  // numCols * cellSize\n  height: number; // numRows * cellSize\n  dpr: number;    // window.devicePixelRatio\n  cellSize: number; // 18px (mobile) or 20px (desktop)\n}\n```\n\n**Rendering Pipeline:**\n1. Canvas Resize: Update width/height if dimensions changed\n2. Transform Reset: Clear and apply DPR scaling\n3. Draw Loop:\n   - Clear canvas with background color\n   - Draw grid lines (if enabled)\n   - Draw live cells with age-based styling and glow\n4. Intensity Update: Set CSS variable `--life-intensity`\n\n**Performance Optimizations:**\n- DPR scaling for sharp rendering using `window.devicePixelRatio`\n- Transform reset before resize\n- Minimized context state changes\n- `useCallback` on dependencies `[numRows, numCols, cellSize]`\n- `requestAnimationFrame` for animations\n\n### Edge Cases & Constraints\n\n1. **Canvas Resize**: Must handle width/height update, DPR scaling, and cell size recalculation together\n2. **Empty Grid**: Draws only grid lines (if enabled)\n3. **High Cell Count**: May have performance issues with 500+ cells\n4. **Rapid Cell Size Changes**: Color computations cached per frame\n\n### Dependencies\n\n- **Core simulation engine**: Provides grid state and dimensions\n- **UI/overlay system**: Grid line toggle setting\n- **User interaction system**: Triggers redraws on cell changes\n\n### Implementation Status: FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n\n**Implemented in:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/CanvasGrid.tsx`\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/canvasUtils.ts`\n\n**What's implemented:**\n- Canvas setup with DPR scaling\n- Age-based cell colors and glow effects\n- Responsive cell sizing (18px mobile, 20px desktop)\n- Toggleable grid lines with G key shortcut\n- Grid lines visibility controlled by phase (PLANNING = visible, RUNNING = hidden)\n- Rounded rectangle cells with 2px corner radius\n- Intensity metric via CSS variable\n- Cell animations (birth fade-in, death shrink-out)\n- Invalid action visualization (red outline)\n- Accessibility: `role=\"img\"` and dynamic `aria-label`\n- Optimized rendering with useCallback\n- Mobile support: `touch-action: none`\n\n**Test Coverage:**\n- Unit tests for `getCellColor()` (age 0-10)\n- Unit tests for `getCellBlur()` (age 0-10)\n- Unit tests for `getResponsiveCellSize()` (desktop/mobile)\n\n**What's MISSING:**\n- None - all spec requirements are implemented\n\n---\n\n## 2. Grid Interaction (`specs/grid-interaction.md`)\n\n### Core Functionality Requirements\n\n**Placement Mode (PLANNING Phase):**\n- Click to place: Single click on empty grid cell places a live cell\n- Click to remove: Single click on existing live cell removes it and refunds Flux\n- Minimum cells rule: START button disabled until at least 1 cell has been placed\n- Interaction modes: DRAW vs ERASE\n\n**Interaction Constraints:**\n- Disabled entirely during RUNNING phase\n- Disabled during FINISHED phase\n- Grid cells must be clickable on both desktop (mouse) and mobile (touch)\n- Touch targets minimum 44x44px for mobile accessibility\n\n**Coordinate System:**\n```typescript\ninterface GridInteraction {\n  cellX: number;        // 0 to gridWidth-1\n  cellY: number;        // 0 to gridHeight-1\n  isPlaceable: boolean; // Calculated based on Flux and existing cell\n}\n```\n\n### UI/UX Requirements\n\n**Cursor States:**\n- **Default**: Standard cursor\n- **Over Empty Cell (Placeable)**: Crosshair\n- **Over Empty Cell (Unplaceable)**: Forbidden symbol (Flux = 0)\n- **Over Live Cell (Removable)**: Crosshair\n\n**Visual Feedback:**\n- **Cell Preview**: Ghost/outline of cell follows cursor when hovering over grid\n- **Cell Placement**: Fade-in animation (0.1s / 100ms duration)\n- **Cell Removal**: Shrink animation (0.15s / 150ms duration)\n- **Invalid Action**: Brief red flash on cursor location (200ms duration)\n\n**Keyboard Accessibility:**\n- Arrow keys for navigation\n- Enter/Space to place/remove cells\n- Escape to clear focus\n\n**Mobile Considerations:**\n- Pinch-to-zoom disabled on game grid\n- Single tap only (no touch-and-hold drag needed)\n- Prevent accidental browser zoom on double-tap\n- Touch coordinates mapped to canvas space\n\n### Edge Cases & Constraints\n\n1. **Rapid Clicking**: User might click faster than animation - ensure state consistency\n2. **Edge of Grid**: Clicking exactly on grid boundary should round to nearest cell\n3. **Overlapping with UI**: Ensure grid doesn't extend under HUD elements\n4. **Window Resize**: Grid cells must maintain aspect ratio on resize\n\n### Technical Implementation Notes\n\n- Use event delegation for grid click handling\n- Calculate cell coordinates from mouse/touch position: `cellX = Math.floor((x - gridOffsetX) / cellSize)`\n- Canvas-based rendering for performance with many cells\n- Implement hit testing to distinguish between grid cells and gaps\n\n### Dependencies\n\n- **Flux management system**: Validates placement/removal, handles refunds\n- **Phase management system**: Enables/disables interaction based on phase\n- **Canvas rendering system**: Visualizes grid, animations, and cursor feedback\n- **Audio sonification system**: Provides feedback sounds for actions\n\n### Implementation Status: FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n\n**Implemented in:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GridInteraction.tsx`\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/interaction.ts`\n\n**What's implemented:**\n- Click-to-place and click-to-remove functionality\n- Phase-based interaction enable/disable (PLANNING only)\n- DRAW and ERASE interaction modes\n- Cursor state management (crosshair, not-allowed, default)\n- Visual feedback:\n  - Cell preview with hover outline (cyan for placeable, magenta for removable, red for unplaceable)\n  - Birth animation (100ms fade-in with cubic-bezier ease)\n  - Death animation (150ms shrink-out with quadratic ease)\n  - Invalid action red flash (200ms duration)\n- Flux-based placement validation\n- Flux refund on cell removal (PLANNING phase only)\n- Mouse and touch event handling\n- Coordinate mapping with DPR support\n- Boundary checking\n- Keyboard accessibility:\n  - Arrow keys for navigation\n  - Enter/Space for cell toggle\n  - Escape to clear focus\n  - Visual focus indicator (yellow border with glow)\n- Mobile support:\n  - `touch-action: none` on canvas\n  - Touch coordinate mapping\n- Accessibility: `role=\"grid\"` and descriptive `aria-label`\n- Hover cell tracking state\n\n**Test Coverage:**\n- Unit tests for `getCellFromEvent()` (mouse, touch, offset, DPR)\n- Unit tests for `isWithinBounds()`\n- Unit tests for `createInitialInteractionState()`\n- Component tests for GridInteraction:\n  - Renders without crashing\n  - Disables interaction during RUNNING phase\n  - Disables interaction during COUNTDOWN phase\n  - Enables interaction during PLANNING phase\n\n**What's MISSING:**\n- None - all spec requirements are implemented\n\n---\n\n## COMPARATIVE SUMMARY\n\n| Aspect | Canvas Rendering | Grid Interaction |\n|--------|-----------------|------------------|\n| Status | Fully Implemented | Fully Implemented |\n| Test Coverage | Complete unit tests | Complete unit + component tests |\n| Mobile Support | Full (responsive sizing, touch handling) | Full (touch events, 44x44px targets) |\n| Accessibility | Role=\"img\", aria-label | Role=\"grid\", keyboard navigation |\n| Performance | Optimized with DPR, useCallback, RAF | Event delegation, optimized state |\n| Integration | Works with simulation engine | Works with flux, phase, canvas |\n\n### Integration Points\n\nBoth systems are tightly integrated through:\n1. **GridInteraction component** wraps **CanvasGrid component**\n2. **CanvasGrid** renders the grid, animations, and visual feedback\n3. **GridInteraction** handles user input and state management\n4. Both use the same **cellSize** for consistent coordinate mapping\n5. Both respect the **phase** (PLANNING vs RUNNING) for enabling/disabling features\n\n### Overall Assessment\n\nBoth spec files are fully implemented with comprehensive test coverage. The implementation follows the specs closely with appropriate optimizations for performance, mobile support, and accessibility. All edge cases documented in the specs are handled in the code.\n</task_result>","title":"Study specs for rendering & grid","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_399ffaf83ffe5jq3mzSOofIyIY","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771237822585,"end":1771237916461}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771237925915,"sessionID":"ses_39a00e1f2ffeTfoOwyWI4Ya0up","part":{"id":"prt_c66005056001JXIqWjfcD5LNCL","sessionID":"ses_39a00e1f2ffeTfoOwyWI4Ya0up","messageID":"msg_c65ffaccc001Z1hKDiWgL1gW5p","type":"tool","callID":"call_f59de00ee20b415b86632912","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Study specs for flux & interaction","prompt":"Study these spec files and provide a comprehensive summary of all requirements, features, and technical details:\n\n1. /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/flux-management.md\n2. /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/user-interaction.md\n\nFor each spec, identify:\n- Core functionality requirements\n- Technical implementation details\n- Edge cases and constraints\n- Dependencies on other systems\n- What's already implemented vs what's missing\n\nReturn a detailed summary of your findings.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_399ffaf9bffe8F3EacbHsPLQEw (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nNow let me provide you with a comprehensive summary of both spec files and their implementation status.\n\n---\n\n# COMPREHENSIVE SPEC SUMMARY\n\n## 1. FLUX MANAGEMENT SPEC\n\n### Core Functionality Requirements\n\n**Mechanics:**\n- Each level starts with 20 Flux (configurable via expert settings, range: 5-50)\n- Each cell placement costs exactly 1 Flux (same cost in both PLANNING and PLAYING phases)\n- **Refund Mechanic**: During PLANNING phase, clicking an existing cell removes it and refunds 1 Flux\n- **No Refunds in Play Phase**: Cells placed during RUNNING phase cannot be removed\n- **Zero State**: When Flux reaches 0, placement is disabled with visual/audio feedback\n- **Strategic Resource Management**: Players decide how much Flux to use during planning vs save for play phase\n- Flux resets every level (no carryover between levels)\n\n**State Management Interface:**\n```typescript\ninterface FluxState {\n  current: number;    // Available Flux\n  initial: number;    // Starting amount for level\n  placed: number;     // Total cells placed (for stats)\n  removed: number;    // Total cells removed (for stats)\n}\n```\n\n### Technical Implementation Details\n\n**VALIDATION RULES:**\n- Cannot place cell if Flux < 1\n- Cannot place cell outside grid bounds\n- Refund only applies during PLANNING phase\n- No refunds during RUNNING or FINISHED phases\n- Can place cells during RUNNING phase using saved Flux\n- No remove functionality during RUNNING phase (add-only)\n\n**UI/UX REQUIREMENTS:**\n- **Location**: Bottom center of screen\n- **Visual**: Bar or counter showing current/initial\n- **Color Coding**:\n  - Green/Yellow when plenty remaining\n  - Orange when < 30% remaining\n  - Red when 0 remaining\n- **Animation**: Smooth transitions when values change\n- **Phase Indication**: Always visible in both PLANNING and RUNNING phases\n\n**FEEDBACK SYSTEM:**\n- **Insufficient Resources**: \n  - Audio: Error/denied sound\n  - Visual: Brief red flash on Flux counter\n- **Placement**: \n  - Audio: Soft \"plop\" sound\n  - Visual: Cell appears with fade-in animation\n- **Removal**: \n  - Audio: Suction/remove sound\n  - Visual: Cell shrinks and disappears\n\n### Edge Cases and Constraints\n\n1. **Zero Flux at Start**: If initial Flux is 0, game should warn or prevent level start\n2. **Accidental Removal**: User might misclick during planning - no undo needed since they can just place again\n3. **Lag Between Click and Update**: Ensure Flux decrement is atomic with cell placement to prevent race conditions\n4. **Strategic Decisions**: Players must balance using Flux in planning vs saving for play phase\n5. **Play Phase Placement**: Must coordinate with simulation step to prevent race conditions\n\n### Dependencies on Other Systems\n\n- Core simulation engine: Grid ref and dimensions\n- Audio sonification system: Play interaction sounds\n- Phase management system: PLANNING vs RUNNING phase state\n- Canvas rendering system: Redraw on state change\n- Settings system: Expert configuration for initial Flux values\n\n### Implementation Status: ALREADY IMPLEMENTED\n\n**FULLY IMPLEMENTED FEATURES:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/flux.ts` - Complete flux logic including:\n  - `createInitialFluxState()` - Creates initial state with configurable Flux\n  - `canPlaceCell()` - Validates Flux availability\n  - `canRefundCell()` - Phase-based refund validation\n  - `placeCell()` - Decrements Flux and tracks placement stats\n  - `removeCell()` - Increments Flux and tracks removal stats\n  - `resetFlux()` - Resets Flux for new levels\n  - `getFluxColor()` - Color coding based on Flux level\n\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/FluxDisplay.tsx` - Complete UI component:\n  - Animated counter display\n  - Smooth value transitions with easing\n  - Color-coded display (green/orange/red)\n  - Accessibility features (aria-live, aria-atomic)\n  - Motion reduction support\n\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/settings.ts` - Expert settings:\n  - Flux configuration: `baseFlux: 20` with range 5-50\n  - Validation for Flux values in expert settings\n\n- Integration with Game component for Flux state management\n- Integration with SoundEngine for error feedback\n- Test coverage in `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/flux.test.ts`\n\n**MINOR ISSUES FOUND:**\n1. CSS missing `.yellow` class in `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/styles/FluxDisplay.css` (line 19 of FluxDisplay component references 'yellow' but CSS only has green, orange, red)\n2. Flux display shows both current/max format as specified\n\n---\n\n## 2. USER INTERACTION SPEC\n\n### Core Functionality Requirements\n\n**INTERACTION MODES:**\n```typescript\ntype InteractionMode = 'draw' | 'erase';\n```\n\n**Draw Mode**: Click/drag to place live cells (age=1)\n**Erase Mode**: Click/drag to remove cells (set to 0)\n\n**MOUSE INTERACTION:**\n\n**Mouse Down:**\n1. Capture mouse position relative to canvas\n2. Convert to grid coordinates: `c = floor(x / (canvasWidth / numCols))`\n3. Trigger interaction handler with type='down'\n\n**Mouse Move (while pressed):**\n1. Capture mouse position\n2. Convert to grid coordinates\n3. Trigger interaction handler with type='enter'\n\n**Mouse Up (global):**\n1. Set `isMouseDown` state to false\n2. Prevent stale drag state\n\n**TOUCH INTERACTION:**\n\n**Touch Start:**\n1. Prevent default (stop scrolling)\n2. Capture first touch position\n3. Convert to grid coordinates\n4. Trigger interaction handler with type='down'\n\n**Touch Move:**\n1. Prevent default (stop scrolling)\n2. Capture first touch position\n3. Convert to grid coordinates\n4. Trigger interaction handler with type='enter'\n\n**Touch End / Cancel:**\n1. Set `isMouseDown` state to false\n\n### Technical Implementation Details\n\n**COORDINATE MAPPING:**\n```typescript\ninterface GridCoordinates {\n  row: number; // 0 to numRows-1\n  col: number; // 0 to numCols-1\n}\n\nfunction getCellFromEvent(\n  event: MouseEvent | TouchEvent,\n  canvas: HTMLCanvasElement,\n  numRows: number,\n  numCols: number\n): GridCoordinates\n```\n\n**INTERACTION HANDLER:**\n```typescript\nfunction handleCellInteract(\n  row: number,\n  col: number,\n  type: 'down' | 'enter'\n): void\n```\n\n- **type='down'**: Modify cell(s)\n- **type='enter'**: Only modify if mouse down\n\n**SOUND INTEGRATION:**\n- Draw/Erase: Play interaction sound (different tones)\n- Sound Engine: Called per cell interaction\n\n**VISUAL FEEDBACK:**\n- Cursor: `crosshair` style over canvas\n- Hover Effects: None (draw directly on grid)\n- Selection Feedback: No preview shown (immediate drawing)\n- Color-coded hover indicator: Cyan for placeable, magenta for removable, red for invalid\n\n### Edge Cases and Constraints\n\n1. **Boundary Coordinates**: Math.floor() ensures valid indices\n2. **Rapid Clicking**: Multiple clicks allowed\n3. **Canvas Resize**: Grid dimensions update, coordinates recalculate\n4. **Touch Conflicts**: PreventDefault() blocks browser zoom/scroll\n5. **Mouse Leave Canvas**: Set isMouseDown to false to stop drag\n\n### Mobile Considerations\n\n- **Touch Action**: `touch-action: none` on canvas element\n- **Target Size**: Responsive cell size (18px mobile, 20px desktop) meets minimum touch target\n- **Prevent Default**: Stop scrolling while drawing\n- **Multi-touch**: Only first touch used (ignore additional touches)\n\n### Dependencies on Other Systems\n\n- Core simulation engine: Grid ref and dimensions\n- Audio sonification system: Play interaction sounds\n- Canvas rendering system: Redraw on state change\n- Flux management system: Validate placement availability\n- Phase management system: Enable/disable interaction based on phase\n\n### Implementation Status: PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED\n\n**FULLY IMPLEMENTED FEATURES:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/interaction.ts` - Core interaction logic:\n  - `getCellFromEvent()` - Mouse and touch event to grid coordinate conversion\n  - `isWithinBounds()` - Boundary validation\n  - `createInitialInteractionState()` - Initial state management\n\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GridInteraction.tsx` - Complete interaction component:\n  - Mouse and touch event handling\n  - Click-based cell placement/removal\n  - Flux integration (checks availability before placement)\n  - Phase-aware interaction (PLANNING only)\n  - Visual feedback with hover indicators\n  - Keyboard navigation (arrow keys, Enter, Space, Escape)\n  - Cell animations (birth/death)\n  - Invalid action feedback (red border)\n\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/CanvasGrid.tsx` - Canvas rendering:\n  - Canvas with `touch-action: none` CSS\n  - Responsive cell sizing\n  - Animation support\n  - Device pixel ratio handling\n\n**MISSING FEATURES:**\n\n1. **DRAG INTERACTION** - The spec mentions \"Click/drag\" but only click is implemented:\n   - Mouse drag drawing is not implemented\n   - Touch drag drawing is not implemented\n   - The `isMouseDown` state is defined but never used for drag-drawing\n   - Only single-click interactions are functional\n\n2. **Spec explicitly states:**\n   - \"Mouse Move (while pressed): Trigger interaction handler with type='enter'\"\n   - \"type='enter': Only modify if mouse down\"\n   - This drag behavior is not implemented in the current code\n\n**PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED FEATURES:**\n\n1. **Sound Integration**: Sound hooks are in place (`onInteractionSound`, `onFluxErrorSound`) and properly integrated with the SoundEngine, but drag sounds would need to be handled differently (throttled) if drag interaction is added\n\n2. **Testing**: Basic tests exist for coordinate conversion and bounds checking (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/interaction.test.ts`) but drag interaction tests would be missing\n\n---\n\n## SUMMARY TABLE\n\n| Feature | Flux Management | User Interaction |\n|---------|----------------|------------------|\n| Core Logic | ✅ Fully Implemented | ⚠️ Partial (drag missing) |\n| UI Components | ✅ Fully Implemented | ✅ Fully Implemented |\n| Audio Feedback | ✅ Fully Implemented | ✅ Fully Implemented |\n| Touch Support | N/A | ✅ Fully Implemented |\n| Mobile Responsive | ✅ Fully Implemented | ✅ Fully Implemented |\n| Accessibility | ✅ Fully Implemented | ✅ Fully Implemented |\n| Test Coverage | ✅ Comprehensive | ⚠️ Partial |\n| Edge Case Handling | ✅ Complete | ⚠️ Drag scenarios missing |\n\n---\n\n## KEY FINDINGS\n\n### Flux Management: 95% Complete\n- Only minor CSS issue (missing yellow class)\n- All core functionality, validation, and feedback systems are implemented\n- Expert settings integration complete\n\n### User Interaction: 70% Complete\n- **Critical Missing Feature**: Drag-to-draw/erase functionality\n- Spec explicitly requires drag interaction but only click is implemented\n- All other features (touch, keyboard, visual feedback, sound) are complete\n- Would need to add drag state management and throttled interaction handling\n\n### Recommendations:\n1. Add drag interaction to GridInteraction component with rate limiting to prevent excessive Flux consumption\n2. Fix missing `.yellow` class in FluxDisplay.css\n3. Add comprehensive drag interaction tests\n4. Consider debouncing rapid drag events for better performance\n</task_result>","title":"Study specs for flux & interaction","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_399ffaf9bffe8F3EacbHsPLQEw","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771237822562,"end":1771237925912}}}}
